WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.500
This is the Far East Region Recovery Squad, Team Gran Seil.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.110
Headquarters, please come in.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.990
Damn, this is useless!

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.460
Is the noise from those insect bastards so high that we can't even use the relay facilities?

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.590
These latest battles have made recovery all over Japan hopeless.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:19.500
Consequently, as for our route from here...

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.030
we'll use these vehicles to get us to Shimonoseki,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.270
then procure a cargo ship and cross over to Korea,

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.270
and join up with the recovery squad there. You'll conduct the fighting.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.210
Sir.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:53.540
Let's go!

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:57.560
Something's coming.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:58.590
Huh?

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:05.880
It's a Blue!

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.150
Go!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.630
It's too dangerous! Get back!

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.210
Dammit!

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.240
I can just as well...

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.930
...it's still clinging on!

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.460
You go to hell!

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.900
Are... are you all right?

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.920
...I thought I told you to stay back.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.240
I wanted to fight too.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.900
Are you really sure you're prepared to do that?

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:21.070
If you amateurs could be winners on your feelings alone, who would ever work at it?

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.540
Training?

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.840
As it is, I'm just baggage right now.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.210
Teach me what it is I should do to fight!

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.220
Do you know what you're saying?

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:03.620
I know I'm an amateur. But I hate it.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.550
As it is, with me not being able to do anything,

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.030
I would absolutely hate to get killed by those things!!

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:16.430
I don't want to ask for help or be treated like a baby, so let me fight!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:17.400
No way.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:18.900
But...

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:24.540
Delivering you to the station alive... that is what our duty is.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:27.600
We can't let you die because you got carried away.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:46.190
Come on, why don't we let him try it?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.000
After all, Robert's in the shape he's in,

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.900
and it'll be too hard to fight our way through what's ahead

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:53.530
in a Fighter without an Arm Pilot.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:56.630
If I take the time to teach him to steer, and Marlene,

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.670
you teach him to shoot, don't you think something will turn out?

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.050
Please?

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.890
Fine. If we're going to do this, you've got three days to get it down.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.960
Y- Yeah! I'll do it!

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:35.740
Hey.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.860
Take aim.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.550
Wrong. Your arms are too far forward.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:53.860
Don't aim with your fingertips. Not like that.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.460
I'm working on it, aren't I!?

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.240
What are you doing!?

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:18.550
Got that? Get yourself accustomed to that.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.720
What's the matter? Didn't I just say to get yourself accustomed?

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:36.170
Don't worry, The computer will compensate for you on the fine touches.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:39.640
Just concentrate on getting familiar with the distance to target and your attack timing.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:40.840
Practice will make perfect.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:41.850
Right.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.910
For now, remember the one fundamental among fundamentals even I know...

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.180
don't close your eyes, no matter what.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:48.850
OK.

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:54.260
Our goal is to punch that jungle gym, thirty meters ahead. Let's go!

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.210
What speed!

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.640
Let's do it again!

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:56.550
...keep your eyes open... and punch through...

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.550
Let's go!

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.540
We hit it...

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:21.210
You've got a knack for this.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.610
We hit it!

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:25.780
This is Marlene. We've found a suitable boat.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.810
Assemble at pier number 10.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.550
...lf we dawdle around, the Blue will come for us.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:31.420
Roger.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.000
Quite the antique...

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.950
However, the computer doesn't appear to have died yet.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.920
With a little maintenance, we should get it to work.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.250
How long will it take?

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:03.910
...I can manage something by tomorrow night.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.250
You've got the rest of the night to finish. Understood?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.280
Yes sir!

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:11.600
The two of you resume your duties.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:13.290
Yes sir!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:29.210
I'll continue on sentry duty.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:32.220
Yuji, you start loading the materials we need.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.220
Heh?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:34.550
What's wrong?

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:39.220
Nothing... I was just thinking that's the first time you called me by my name is all.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:42.590
It'd be inconvenient not to use your name.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:11.290
Huh?

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:16.250
Hm? Something wrong?

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.260
That song you're humming...

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:20.600
How do you know it?

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:25.800
It was popular among the guys in my class. I've taken a liking to it.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:36.880
I like that song too.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:37.540
You too?

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.210
That song is one that comes from my era.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:43.550
Yeah?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:46.890
Pretty old song then, huh?

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:52.560
It went around my city a lot. The city where my dad, and my mom, and my friends...

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:55.900
...that's where we all lived.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.370
I made a promise to one of them...

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:03.240
that no matter how many years had passed, we'd meet again in the future world.

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:07.110
And so I can't very well break my promise to him by dying...

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:11.910
No matter what... I can't go getting killed, my face full of tears...

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.920
Uh huh...

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.410
So you guys know the song too, hmm?

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.590
...No, that part there is different.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:26.930
Really?

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.360
Like this-

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:16.240
The repairs are complete.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:20.150
Prepare for departure!! Marlene, keep your eyes open!!

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.530
Blue approaching!

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.540
Have they sniffed us out already!?

00:15:41.570 --> 00:15:45.200
I'm reading three... no, four, there are four of them.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:48.210
Intercept them! Marlene has command of the battle.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:51.220
Right! Just watch us!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.510
Yuji, Joey!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:55.280
Looks as though three of them are the aerial type.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:58.550
You guys take the Blue on land on our right wing.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:03.220
Focus on keeping it bottled up until I can shoot down the flying ones.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.890
By no means get into a fight beyond what you can handle.

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.900
Bottled up...

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:11.230
It's not as easy as you think to kill these Blue... If you want to die, feel free.

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:12.900
All right!

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:15.240
Commencing attack!

00:16:15.270 --> 00:16:17.270
We're off too!

00:16:46.870 --> 00:16:49.470
It's all right. After all...

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.840
After all that practice I've had...

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:54.370
If I can stay calm and fight, we'll beat it for sure.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:57.440
So then, where's the bastard hiding?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:02.220
I'm not going to be deceived... Come on out... Come out now!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.480
Yuji... Yuji!

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.890
Calm down! You can't be so anxious.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:09.550
I am calm!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.220
You've been told that you must not force it, right?

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.130
I know!

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:15.160
Above us!

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:40.190
No way!

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.250
Shit!

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.880
Are you really sure you're prepared to do that?

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.550
If you amateurs could be winners on your feelings alone, who would ever work at it?

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:15.220
I'm not going to die.

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:17.250
I'm not going to die!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.970
Hm?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:44.180
If we keep going at this pace, we'll arrive at the Korean coast sometime tomorrow.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:45.310
Right.

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:57.530
Where are we?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:04.530
We're joining up with the Korean recovery squad.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:05.870
Where's Joey?

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:10.530
Joey's begun repairs on the Fighter by now. You go too.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.670
All right.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:39.690
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:45.820
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:54.970
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:55.090 --> 00:22:01.140
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:07.560
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:14.750
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:19.910
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:25.970
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:32.250
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:39.730
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:46.590
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:54.770
Kaido Yuji, let me warn you about one thing...

00:22:54.810 --> 00:22:58.970
if you want to get out of here alive, mind your own business.

00:23:02.180 --> 00:23:06.680
The lives and deaths of the people left on Earth are unimportant to our operation...

00:23:07.600 --> 00:23:13.010
That's right... consider the people here as already being dead.
